{#
  implement.j2 — code/file mutation prompt.

  Purpose: instruct an agent to apply a change to the worktree, with tests
  where appropriate. Typically used in nodes with `writes_files: true` and
  an empty contract (`writes: []`); the agent calls submit with `{}` to
  signal completion.

  Required template_vars:
    task         - what to implement (string)

  Optional template_vars:
    constraints  - additional constraints (e.g. "no new deps"); omitted by default
    submit_tool_name - name of the submit tool injected by the contract;
                       defaults to "submit" so this template renders standalone.
#}
{{ task }}

Apply the change. Write or update tests where the change is testable; run them and confirm they pass before submitting. Keep the diff focused — no drive-by refactors.
{% if constraints is defined %}
Constraints: {{ constraints }}
{% endif %}
When the work is complete and verified, call {{ submit_tool_name | default('submit') }} exactly once. If the contract is empty, call {{ submit_tool_name | default('submit') }} with no arguments — the file mutations are the output.
